schema: "0.4"
id: npl-ux-d4-topbar-bento-settings-keys
type: image
quality: high

# Direction D4: top-bar only + bento home — screen: org settings key vault, reveal-once/rotate/last-used rows, invite cap meter
# Nocturne palette (exact hexes, dark-native canvas — never pure #000/#fff): canvas #010409, panel #0d1117, raised #161b22, border #21262d, primary text #e6edf3 (soft off-white ink), secondary text #909dab, muted text #6e7681, signal green (live/primary accent) #3fb950, link cyan (navigation) #58a6ff, amber (rare warning) #d29922, error coral #f85149. Type: Inter for UI/labels, JetBrains Mono (co-equal voice) for counts, timestamps, ids, code, SQL, paths. Shape: flat surfaces separated by lightness steps only, 4px radius, no drop shadows, no glow, no gradients, no neon bloom, no OLED pitch-black, no pure-white surfaces.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity dark-native app UI
    for NoizuPromptLingo. This direction has NO SIDEBAR AT ALL: navigation lives
    entirely in a persistent TOP BAR (org switcher, primary destinations as
    horizontal tabs/links, search, notifications, user menu). Section landing
    pages and the home screen are BENTO grids of tiles. Render as a real product
    screenshot, never a wireframe.
  text: |
        A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of NoizuPromptLingo's Settings / Key Vault
        screen, testing the TOP-BAR-ONLY shell direction — NO left sidebar.

        TOP BAR (IDENTICAL structure and IDENTICAL labels to the paired home
        shot): far left an org switcher ("Acme Robotics ▾") next to a small
        wordmark "NPL"; center-left a horizontal row of EXACTLY EIGHT primary
        destination LINKS as text (not icons), in this EXACT order and with
        this EXACT spelling — no synonyms, no rewording, no additional or
        substitute labels: "Home", "Work", "Chat", "Knowledge", "Files",
        "Data", "Integrations", "Settings". "Settings" is the active item
        (green underline). The eight labels must be spelled exactly as
        listed; no other nav labels. Far right: a search affordance
        ("/ search") with a visible "/" keyboard-shortcut hint, a
        notification bell with a green unread badge, and a user avatar.

        BELOW THE TOP BAR, a SECONDARY IN-PAGE TAB ROW (since there's no
        sidebar, settings sub-sections are horizontal tabs just under the
        header): "General", "Members", "Roles", "Scopes", "Notifications",
        "Keys" (active, green underline), "Danger zone".

        MAIN CONTENT (bento-flavored: a few distinct panel tiles, not one dense
        form): a page title "Key Vault" with a "Generate new key" button
        (green fill, 4px radius). A KEY LIST tile — table-like rows with
        hairline separators: key name ("CI deploy key", "MCP integration key",
        "Backup automation"), a masked mono key preview ("npl_live_••••8f2a"),
        a "Rotate" cyan text action, a "Revoke" coral text action, and a
        mono "Last used" relative timestamp per row. One row shows a fresh key
        with a "Reveal once" green button instead of a masked preview and a
        small warning note "This key will not be shown again" in amber text.

        A separate smaller tile: an INVITE CAP METER — a horizontal progress
        bar (green fill up to ~70%) labeled "Seats used: 14 / 20", with a
        muted caption "6 invites remaining this billing cycle".

        Use realistic, specific product content throughout — never lorem ipsum.

  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, neon glow, bloom, CRT scanlines, gradient background, pure-black OLED background, pure-white surfaces, warm amber/gold dominant palette, light-mode canvas"

attachments:
  - path: _nocturne-palette.png
    role: reference
    description: "Locked Nocturne palette swatches (bg, surface, border, text, muted, accent, success, danger) with hex labels — match these exact colors, do not reinterpret."

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

service: gemini
provider_options:
  generate_content_model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Shows the same sidebar-free top bar with exactly the eight labels Home, Work, Chat, Knowledge, Files, Data, Integrations, Settings in that exact order and spelling (Settings active), a secondary in-page tab row with Keys active, a key vault list with masked keys, rotate/revoke actions, a reveal-once fresh key with an amber warning note, and an invite-cap progress meter tile"}
    consistent_top_bar: {weight: 2, description: "Top bar nav labels exactly match the eight specified labels and order, identical in structure to the paired home-bento shot"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Dark-native Nocturne canvas (#010409/#0d1117), single phosphor-green #3fb950 signal, link cyan #58a6ff, amber #d29922 used sparingly, mono-first counts/timestamps/ids in JetBrains Mono, 4px radius, flat surface-step elevation, no shadow/glow/gradient"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "No sidebar anywhere, clear two-tier navigation (top bar + in-page tabs), key list and invite meter read as distinct bento-style tiles"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "neon glow, bloom, or gradient wash"
    - "light-mode or warm/gold dominant canvas instead of dark-native Nocturne"
    - "nav labels differ from the eight specified"

tags: [ux-overhaul, npl-nocturne, NoizuPromptLingo, shell-direction, direction-4]
